  "conclusion": "Warm delivery declined from 59.37 to 51.73 updates/s as whole JPEG CPU/update rose from 7.98 to 19.33 ms. Across selected jobs, CPU/instruction rose 97.22% despite fewer instructions/job, with unchanged sampled worker policy. This supports an execution-efficiency component and a bounded parallelism experiment; it does not prove the underlying hardware cause or that four workers fix it.",
